# Build-time public IDs, committed on purpose.
#
# `web/.env` is gitignored, so a CI build never sees it — and CI is what
# actually publishes: `.github/workflows/daily-publish.yml` runs `npm ci &&
# npm run build` and deploys Hosting every night. Keeping these only in the
# local `.env` meant the nightly build silently shipped a bundle with GA
# disabled and no ad units, overwriting whatever a manual deploy had put there.
# That is how GA4 ended up recording nothing but the default page view from
# index.html's inline tag: `analytics.ts` reads VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID, found
# "", and every trackPageView/trackEvent call became a no-op (verified 2026-08-07
# against the live bundle, which contained neither ID).
#
# Nothing here is a secret. All three are visible in the shipped bundle and in
# the rendered ad tag, and the first two are already committed in index.html.
# Real secrets stay in `.env` / Cloud Run env and must never move here.
#
# Vite loads this file for `npm run build` and it takes precedence over `.env`,
# so this is the file to edit when changing what production ships.

VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XC1KSGMXTX

# AdSense: all three conditions in AdSlot.tsx must hold or units stay collapsed —
# APPROVED true, client starting `ca-pub-`, and a digits-only slot.
VITE_ADSENSE_CLIENT=ca-pub-5313547246984797
VITE_ADSENSE_SLOT=3080452262
VITE_ADSENSE_APPROVED=true
